::heading Getting Started with dx

::paragraph
Build sites, systems, and docs. Write them as structured blocks. Render to see them live. Inspect and edit any part—no copy-paste needed.

::heading Here's What It Looks Like

::paragraph
This showcase demonstrates what you can create. Click any block to edit it inline:

::view src=examples/showcase.dx

::heading Install (One Command)

::paragraph
If you have Rust installed:

::code run
dx setup

::paragraph
This installs dx, registers your document viewer, and configures your browser for live editing.

::heading Quick Start (Five Lines)

::code
mkdir my-docs && cd my-docs
git init
echo "::heading\nWelcome" > README.dx
dx serve
# Open http://localhost:5000 in your browser

::heading What You Can Build

