- Full format guide: CLAUDE.md § What this is

::heading How It Works

::paragraph
A .dx file is a structured document made of blocks: headings, paragraphs, code, diagrams, and more. Write the source, render it to a page, and click any part to edit. The same renderer lives in the CLI, VS Code, and your browser—so a site looks identical everywhere.

::paragraph
Documents are stored in a compressed chunk store and version-controlled with git. Every read—an editor, the CLI, an agent—goes through the store and gets the true content, byte-for-byte identical.

::paragraph
Code blocks can run in a sandbox. You define inputs and dependencies, and each block executes isolated from your machine, showing output inline.

::paragraph
Boards are node editors on the page. You drag boxes, draw connections, and edit each node without leaving the document. No separate diagram tool.

::paragraph
Everything stays in plain text and version control. No database. No proprietary format. Just .dx files, a store, and one rendering engine.
